---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';

const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const linkedInUrl = 'REPLACE_WITH_LINKEDIN_URL';
const cvUrl = 'REPLACE_WITH_CV_URL';

const withBase = (href: string) => (href === '/' ? baseUrl : `${baseUrl}${href.replace(/^\//, '')}`);
---

<Layout
	title="About Carlos Jorques - Embedded Control Systems Architect"
	description="About Carlos Jorques, an Embedded Control Systems Architect working across automotive embedded software, real-time control, diagnostics, safety-related development, validation, and technical leadership."
>
	<section class="section about-hero">
		<div class="about-shell">
			<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
			<h1>Hi, I'm Carlos.</h1>
			<div class="about-hero__copy">
				<p class="lead">
					I lead technical teams designing real-time control and embedded software for
					physical systems, from electrified vehicles to autonomous machines.
				</p>
				<p>
					My work sits where control engineering, embedded software, diagnostics, and
					production delivery meet. I focus on systems that must behave efficiently, safely,
					and predictably under real-world conditions.
				</p>
			</div>
			<nav class="about-link-row" aria-label="About page links">
				<a href={withBase('/cases')}>View selected work</a>
				<a href={withBase('/writing')}>Read writing</a>
				<a href={withBase('/contact')}>Contact</a>
				<a href={linkedInUrl}>LinkedIn</a>
				<a href={cvUrl}>CV</a>
			</nav>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section about-profile" aria-labelledby="profile-title">
		<div class="about-shell">
			<div class="section-intro">
				<p class="eyebrow">Profile</p>
				<h2 id="profile-title">Embedded control systems architect and technical leader</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="profile-panel">
				<p class="profile-panel__lead">
					Best matched to roles where control systems, embedded software, diagnostics,
					safety-related development, validation, and team execution need to move together.
				</p>
				<p>
					I have more than 10 years of experience in automotive embedded control systems,
					with work across electrified, hybrid, and combustion-based platforms. My academic
					background includes PhD-level training in real-time control and diagnostics,
					supported by a foundation in automatic control, optimization, signal processing,
					modeling, and experimental validation.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section about-origin" aria-labelledby="origin-title">
		<div class="about-shell">
			<div class="section-intro">
				<p class="eyebrow">Origin</p>
				<h2 id="origin-title">Where it started</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="story-prose">
				<p>
					My interest in engineering began with taking things apart. I was the child who
					opened toys and devices simply to understand how they worked. That curiosity drew
					me toward electronics and robotics, where mechanics, electronics, and computation
					come together.
				</p>
				<p>
					I learned to see intelligent machines not by how they look, but by how they sense,
					respond, act, and adapt to their environment. Since then, I have spent my career
					learning how to design systems that can do exactly that.
				</p>
				<blockquote>Long before I knew control theory, I was already thinking in feedback loops.</blockquote>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section about-approach" aria-labelledby="approach-title">
		<div class="about-shell">
			<div class="section-intro">
				<p class="eyebrow">Approach</p>
				<h2 id="approach-title">Turning uncertainty into decisions</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="story-prose">
				<p>
					As engineering challenges become more complex, curiosity alone is not enough.
					When clear answers are not available, curiosity becomes the entry point to
					systematic exploration: turning questions into models, models into evidence, and
					evidence into decisions.
				</p>
				<p>
					For me, innovation moves between fast discovery and disciplined delivery.
					Discovery reduces uncertainty by revealing how systems behave and where
					engineering effort creates the most leverage. Delivery is where those insights
					must survive real-time constraints, safety requirements, legacy systems,
					validation evidence, and team collaboration.
				</p>
				<blockquote>The tools evolve. The loop stays the same.</blockquote>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section about-work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
		<div class="about-shell">
			<div class="section-intro">
				<p class="eyebrow">Work</p>
				<h2 id="work-title">Systems where software has physical consequences</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="story-prose">
				<p>
					I work on engineered systems where software decisions have physical consequences.
				</p>
				<p>
					These systems operate continuously in the real world, run under uncertainty, and
					cannot fail silently. My focus is real-time control and embedded software for
					dynamic systems such as electrified powertrains, battery systems, combustion
					engines, thermal systems, and autonomous machines.
				</p>
				<p>
					From predictive thermal management to traction and motion control, I help shape
					architectures that balance efficiency, safety, robustness, and production readiness.
				</p>
				<blockquote>Different domains, same challenge: turning complex behavior into systems that can be trusted.</blockquote>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section about-leadership" aria-labelledby="leadership-title">
		<div class="about-shell">
			<div class="section-intro">
				<p class="eyebrow">Leadership</p>
				<h2 id="leadership-title">Creating the conditions for good engineering</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="story-prose">
				<p>
					I lead by creating the conditions for engineers to do their best work: clarity,
					context, autonomy, accountability, and constructive collaboration.
				</p>
				<p>
					That means making decisions explicit, connecting architecture with implementation,
					protecting execution time, removing blockers, and ensuring the right information
					reaches the right people at the right time.
				</p>
				<p>
					I value T-shaped engineers, open dialogue, and cross-functional perspectives. The
					goal is not only to deliver reliable software in production, but to build teams
					that improve with every release.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section about-background" aria-labelledby="background-title">
		<div class="about-shell">
			<div class="section-intro">
				<p class="eyebrow">Background</p>
				<h2 id="background-title">From automatic control to production embedded systems</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="story-prose">
				<p>
					My foundation combines industrial engineering, electrical engineering, and
					automatic control. Automatic control became the discipline that connected my
					interest in robotics, dynamic systems, electronics, and software.
				</p>
				<p>
					During my Industrial PhD, I worked on model-based diagnostics and closed-loop
					control for complex physical systems. That period shaped how I think about
					observers, estimation, signal processing, stochastic behavior, system modeling,
					experimental validation, and the relationship between research ideas and
					production constraints.
				</p>
				<p>
					Professionally, my work has moved from combustion control, diagnostics, and
					thermal systems toward electrification, battery-related software, charging
					interfaces, propulsion behavior, and autonomous machine contexts. Over time, my
					role has evolved from algorithm development to architecture, technical direction,
					mentoring, and team leadership.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section about-technical" aria-labelledby="technical-title">
		<div class="about-shell">
			<div class="section-intro">
				<p class="eyebrow">Technical context</p>
				<h2 id="technical-title">The work behind the profile</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="technical-grid" aria-label="Technical context areas">
				<article>
					<span>Control and modeling</span>
					<p>Predictive and optimal control, estimation, signal processing, simulation, and validation.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<span>Embedded implementation</span>
					<p>Model-based software, real-time constraints, C/C++, generated code, integration, and maintainability.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<span>Production delivery</span>
					<p>Requirements, architecture, safety-related development, diagnostics, CI/CD, MIL/SIL/HIL, and field validation.</p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section about-fit" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
		<div class="about-shell">
			<div class="fit-panel">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">Best fit</p>
					<h2 id="fit-title">Where I am most useful</h2>
				</div>
				<p>
					I am most useful in roles involving embedded control systems architecture for
					vehicles and intelligent machines; automotive embedded software, diagnostics, and
					model-based development; safety-related development and validation; and technical
					leadership across controls, software, systems, suppliers, and stakeholders.
				</p>
				<p>
					The common thread is software that must reflect a deep understanding of the
					physical system it controls.
				</p>
				<nav class="about-link-row about-link-row--compact" aria-label="Best fit links">
					<a href={withBase('/cases')}>View selected work</a>
					<a href={withBase('/writing')}>Read writing</a>
					<a href={withBase('/contact')}>Contact</a>
					<a href={linkedInUrl}>LinkedIn</a>
					<a href={cvUrl}>CV</a>
				</nav>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section about-contact">
		<div class="about-shell">
			<ContactCTA
				title="Need embedded control architecture, automotive software leadership, or production control systems depth?"
				body="Contact me for technical leadership roles, embedded control systems architecture, model-based automotive software, diagnostics, or control intelligence for physical systems."
			/>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.about-shell {
		width: min(100% - 48px, var(--content-narrow));
		margin-inline: auto;
	}

	.about-hero {
		padding-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
	}

	.about-hero h1 {
		max-width: 820px;
		margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
		font-size: clamp(2.45rem, 6vw, 5rem);
		line-height: 1;
	}

	.about-hero__copy,
	.story-prose {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		max-width: 760px;
		color: var(--color-muted);
		font-size: 1rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.about-hero__copy .lead {
		color: var(--color-text);
		font-size: clamp(1.22rem, 2.4vw, 1.65rem);
		line-height: 1.35;
	}

	.about-link-row {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.65rem 1rem;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.about-link-row a {
		color: var(--color-text);
		text-decoration: none;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
		padding-bottom: 0.12rem;
	}

	.about-link-row a:hover,
	.about-link-row a:focus-visible {
		color: var(--color-accent);
	}

	.about-link-row--compact {
		margin-top: 0.4rem;
	}

	.about-profile,
	.about-origin,
	.about-approach,
	.about-work,
	.about-leadership,
	.about-background,
	.about-technical,
	.about-fit,
	.about-contact {
		padding-top: 0;
	}

	.section-intro {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.55rem;
		max-width: 760px;
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
	}

	.section-intro h2,
	.fit-panel h2 {
		font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 3vw, 2.35rem);
		line-height: 1.12;
	}

	.profile-panel,
	.fit-panel {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		padding: 1.25rem;
	}

	.profile-panel p,
	.fit-panel p,
	.technical-grid p {
		color: var(--color-muted);
		font-size: 0.96rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
	}

	.profile-panel__lead {
		color: var(--color-text) !important;
		font-size: 1.1rem !important;
		line-height: 1.5 !important;
	}

	blockquote {
		margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
		border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
		padding: 0.2rem 0 0.2rem 1rem;
		color: var(--color-text);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
		line-height: 1.55;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.technical-grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		background: var(--color-border);
	}

	.technical-grid article {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.45rem;
		background: var(--color-page);
		padding: 1.05rem 0;
	}

	.technical-grid span {
		color: var(--color-accent);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		line-height: 1.25;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.about-contact :global(.contact-cta) {
		grid-template-columns: 1fr;
	}

	@media (min-width: 760px) {
		.technical-grid {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
		}

		.technical-grid article {
			padding: 1.1rem;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.about-shell {
			width: min(100% - 32px, var(--content-narrow));
		}

		.profile-panel,
		.fit-panel {
			padding: 1rem;
		}
	}
</style>
